    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Taking Senya's advice literally, Denis bumps into waiter Nikita in the hotel corridor and warns him not to hit on Katya. Listen to their brief confrontation.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "Что это было? Извините.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "Глаза открой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извини, я случайно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Слушай, я к тебе пришёл.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я пришёл на самом деле.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты Катю знаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "Кого ты сейчас назвал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нашу Катю с кухни.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я её парень, понял?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не надо к ней приставать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "Чего? Я тебя не понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "О чём ты вообще говоришь?",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "Что это было? Извините.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What was that? Excuse me.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'what' before landing on 'excuse me'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "Глаза открой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Open your eyes.' Nikita brings out the contrast between 'eyes' and 'to open' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извини, я случайно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Sorry, I did it by accident.' Denis anchors the line on 'sorry', while 'by accident' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Слушай, я к тебе пришёл.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Listen, I actually came to see you.' Notice how Russian expresses 'listen' and 'arrived' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я пришёл на самом деле.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I came here for a real reason.' The meaning hinges on 'I' working together with 'practice' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты Катю знаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you know Katya?' Notice how Russian expresses 'you' and 'know' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Nikita answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "Кого ты сейчас назвал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Who did you just name?' The meaning hinges on 'whom' working together with 'called' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нашу Катю с кухни.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Our Katya from the kitchen.' Notice how Russian expresses 'our' and 'kitchen' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я её парень, понял?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am her boyfriend, got it?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'I' before landing on 'understood'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не надо к ней приставать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You should not hit on her.' Denis anchors the line on 'not', while 'to hit on' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "Чего? Я тебя не понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What? I did not understand you.' Nikita anchors the line on 'what', while 'understood' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nikita",
      "t": "О чём ты вообще говоришь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you talking about at all?' Notice how Russian expresses 'about' and 'speak' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
